      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRIS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nThe question presented today is whether a claim for contractual reimbursement is cognizable under section 502(a)(3) of ERISA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Sereboff v. Mid Atlantic Medical Services."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- if the day before the settlement was consummated,\nthe plan had gone into court and had said the -- the\nbeneficiaries plan to settle the case and they've\nindicated that they're not going to give us any of the\nsettlement in accordance with the terms of the contract\nand we want an injunction preventing their distribution\nto anyone but -- but us, if the -- if the judge\nbelieved that and believed that under the contract, the\nplan was entitled to reimbursement, could the judge\nhave enjoined the -- the distribution of the funds to\nthe -- you know, to the extent of the plan's claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But I don't understand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What -- what is the double recovery that you're talking about? The plan has paid out to the care providers the benefits in full."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, did you attempt to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why -- why isn't that what occurred here? What -- what's the essential difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You -- you have piqued my curiosity and -- and didn't satisfy it. You say there are variations on make-whole. What -- you were about to describe the variations. What are the variations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At that point, I want to know how you think this case should come out. What words should be written there if I'm thinking of the next case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying or are you going to say you can't unscramble the eggs consistently with -- with the limitation to equitable remedies, or are you going to say you can unscramble the eggs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. COLEMAN",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe that our plan sufficiently captures the essence of the age-old equitable subrogation right, that in seeking to enforce that plan, we both capture those subrogation-based rights, but our plan also commits to seek funds solely from a fund, a res, that will come into existence as a result of the third party litigation --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James A. Feldman",
      "case_id": "2005-05-260",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "47b949b8aa341b0b4af40b255384988f14adbc057750d57a2330195671650760",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47b949b8aa34-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This -- this case is an action for appropriate equitable relief under this Court's decision in Great-West. First, it seeks a specifically identifiable fund, which is the money that Petitioners got from their tort settlement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
